   ],
   "summary": "Lunar gravity can widen flammability limits: convective heat loss is lower than on Earth while buoyancy still brings fresh oxygen to the flame. SIBAL cotton/fiberglass fabric burns downward in air in lunar gravity (centrifuge and parabolic flight) but goes out immediately on Earth. Partial-gravity aircraft tests also found faster downward spread and lower limiting oxygen as gravity drops from 1 g. FM2 will burn samples on the Moon at 21 % O2/14.7 psia and 34 % O2/8.2 psia.",
